Anyway, here are some Yanis for Items.

1) Swiss knife
Functions as a weapon knife.
Processes tainted meat (produces partly eaten/partly consumed
corpses with less nutrition value but possible intrinsics intact).
Untraps every kind of trap which can be #untrapped, plus exploding tins.
Opens tins in one turn. To prevent abuse, may have n amount of charges
for processing the said tainted meat.
Can be used to "tweak" ie. arrow traps (even previously untrapped traps)
- a monster stepping on a tweaked arrow trap will become a cushion pin
in one turn and the trap is destroyed.

2) A straw
5% chance of getting an usable straw from a straw golem.
Can be used to taste potions, producing diluted potions (it's assumed
that the player spits in the bottle afterwards to keep it full of liquid).
May resist polymorphing if a blessed !oPoly is tasted.
Player can spit poison or acid with the straw (I have myself tested
this method with Coca Cola). Acid will eventually wear out the straw.
Used in shallow water (near shores/beaches), players can breathe underwater,
assuming that player needs air and has a mouth or a suitable breathing orifice.
When spitting oil with the straw and using a lit candle, the player may produce
a flame thrower effect. The fire will eventually wear out the straw.

3) A pair of skates
When worn, may cause fumbling if the player is NOT on ice.
When worn on ice, player gets "fast" -intrinsic (up to very fast).
Kicking damage bonuses.
Engrave E-word while on ice.

4) Pipe
This is what NetHack really needs. Depending on the type of
pipe weed, player can produce smoke rings, small stinking
clouds, illusionary smoke monsters to cause fear to enemies,
trigger hallucination and generally just abuse health.

5) A piano string / a guitar string
Hitman, anyone? With this "tool", the players turn the tide when
it comes to choking living beings! With the string, you can stealthily
assasinate a monster, providing that:
- The monster isn't too large, has a neck and has to breathe air.
- Player has enough strenght and dexterity.
- The monster is asleep/stunned/paralyzed/frightened/blinded.

6) A hook and a rope.
Can be used to drag monsters around (ie. towards altars), maybe
even pull water monsters out of water!
The hook causes damage to monsters but the rope may snap.
Can be used to climb out of pits.

7) The next generation sling: Slingshot.
Can be used to fire stones or gems.
5% chance for piously aligned lawfuls to kill giants with a single shot.
(it'd be a cool feature for ordinary slings, too)

8) Beewax-n-Feather gliding wings.
When not burdened, players can "levitate" for a short
distance... and much farther than by doing a normal jump.
While in midair, players can deal more damage by hitting
the monster from above, assuming that the monster has a head
or any other vital area vulnerable to death from above.
Players can also do a jousting attack by using a lance if they
have enough momentum left during their glide.
An attempt to pull a 180 degree turn will cause the "glider" to stall.
Immense heat will cause the beewax to melt and the feathers
catch fire, sending the player crashing down.

9) Poké Ball
When thrown at a monster, Poké Ball can trap one monster inside
it, providing that the monster doesn't resist. Applying a Ball containing
a monster will release it. A cursed Poké Ball has 1% possibility of
releasing the monster on each turn. Pets inside Poké Balls won't
starve to death, but become less tame every time they're put inside
the Balls.
A "renegade" bouncing Poké Ball could trap (polymorphed) players...
forever.

10) Rubber crocodile
This handy tool can ferry players across waters, but possessions
(including those in BoH) *might* eventually make contact with water.
A cursed rubber crocodile may start deflating due an attack or something
else. Fortunately, the airflow may hurl the player and the crocodile towards
the shore. When applied against a monster, rubber crocodile can scare
monsters that are normally threatened by real crocodiles.

In conclusion, ladies and gentlemen of the jury, I state that we need
more water levels in NetHack, so I can introduce the next YANIs, including
the Torpedo, the Sea Mine, water skis, a sea warning buoy, scuba gear and
fishing equipment (for normal fishing and ice fishing) to name a few.

